<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows $13.1 mln June 10.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows $13.1 mln June 10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $13.1 million deficit on June 10 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 10</p>
<p>Exports: $277.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $231.4 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $358.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $417.2 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $13.1 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.621 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.805 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.757 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.388 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $185 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
